   <p>Beyond the four standard presets, freeform cropping exists for situations that don't map to a common ratio at all — an unusual print size, a specific layout requirement from a design brief, or simply wanting creative control over an unconventional composition. Freeform mode drops the ratio constraint entirely, letting the crop box be dragged and resized to any shape and proportion. This is also the right mode when you know the exact pixel dimensions you need (say, 350×450 for a specific ID card spec) rather than just a ratio — position the crop box freely, then verify the resulting dimensions match your requirement, adjusting a resize step afterward if the exact pixel count still needs fine-tuning.</p>
 
