   <p>The reverse-feeling but equally common question: what is 20% of 150? Here the formula is <code>number × (percentage ÷ 100)</code>, or equivalently, convert the percentage to a decimal and multiply directly: 150 × 0.20 = 30. This calculation is the one behind discount pricing (20% off $150 means subtracting $30), tipping (15% of a $60 bill), and tax calculations (adding a percentage-based tax onto a base price).</p>
 
