   <h2>Conclusion</h2>
   <p>Most resizing problems come down to one setting: keep aspect ratio lock on unless you have a specific reason not to, and always resize down from the largest original you have rather than up from something small. Beyond that, matching your target dimensions to how the image will actually be displayed is the simplest way to avoid both wasted file size and unnecessary quality loss. Getting this right the first time saves the repeated back-and-forth of resizing, checking, and re-resizing that otherwise eats into time better spent elsewhere, and understanding the shrink-versus-enlarge distinction turns a fairly opaque process into a predictable one.</p>
