   <p>The user agent is a text string your browser sends with every web request, originally intended to let servers identify the browser and adjust content accordingly. Over the years, this string has become somewhat messy for historical compatibility reasons — many browsers include references to other browser engines in their user agent for legacy compatibility purposes, which is why parsing it correctly to identify the actual browser in use requires more careful logic than a simple text match might suggest. This tool handles that parsing for you, extracting the actual browser name and version from what can otherwise be a confusingly layered string.</p>
 
