   <p>When both the day-of-month and day-of-week fields are set to specific values rather than *, most cron implementations treat them as an OR condition — the job runs if either condition is true, not only when both match simultaneously. This is a frequently misunderstood part of cron syntax and worth double-checking with the generated explanation before relying on it for a production schedule.</p>
 
   <h3>Common Scheduling Use Cases</h3>
-  <ul class="feature-list">
