   <p>Before cron-style schedulers, recurring tasks had to be triggered manually or through custom scripts with their own timing logic. Cron standardized this into a compact, portable syntax that works the same way across Linux servers, container orchestrators, and many SaaS scheduling features, which is why the same five-field format keeps showing up well beyond traditional Unix systems.</p>
 
   <h3>Common Mistakes with Cron Expressions</h3>
-  <ul class="feature-list">
+  <ul>
