     <li>Disable both options when you need <strong>exact, case-sensitive matching</strong> — useful for things like deduplicating case-sensitive variable names or codes where "ABC" and "abc" genuinely need to be treated as different values.</li>
     <li>Use <strong>sorting</strong> after deduplication when you need to eyeball the result for anything unusual, since an alphabetically sorted list makes it much easier to spot near-duplicates (like a typo'd variant) that the automated matching didn't catch.</li>
