     <h2>What Is URL Deduplication?</h2>
     <p>URL deduplication is the process of taking a list of links and reducing it down to one entry per unique destination. It sounds simple, but "unique" is doing a lot of work in that sentence. A straightforward approach — comparing URL strings character by character — only catches exact duplicates: the same string appearing twice. In practice, most duplicate URLs in a real-world list aren't exact string matches at all. They're near-duplicates: the same underlying page, written slightly differently. <code>https://example.com/pricing</code> and <code>https://example.com/pricing/</code> almost always point to the same page, but as plain text strings they're different. A naive deduplication pass misses that, and a list that should have 500 unique URLs ends up reported as 650.</p>
 
