     <p>This tool uses the Web Crypto API's <code>crypto.subtle.digest()</code> method, a native browser function built specifically for cryptographic operations. For text input, the string is first encoded to raw bytes with <code>TextEncoder</code>; for files, the browser reads the file directly into an <code>ArrayBuffer</code>. That byte data is passed to the digest function, which returns a fixed-length binary hash that's then converted to a readable hexadecimal string. Because this is a native browser API rather than a JavaScript-only implementation, hashing runs quickly even on large files without freezing the page.</p>
 
     <h3>SHA-1 vs SHA-256 vs SHA-384 vs SHA-512</h3>
-    <ul class="feature-list">
+    <ul>
