       <li><strong>SHA-256 (256-bit):</strong> produces a 64-character hex output; the de facto standard for file checksums, Git commit hashes, TLS certificates, and most modern software integrity checks.</li>
       <li><strong>SHA-384 (384-bit):</strong> produces a 96-character hex output; a truncated variant of SHA-512 used where a stronger hash than SHA-256 is wanted without the full SHA-512 length.</li>
