   <p>Watermarking is a simple, low-effort way to protect creative work shared publicly online. Photographers, designers, and content creators commonly add a subtle watermark — a name, logo text, or website URL — to portfolio previews, social media posts, and stock samples, making it harder for others to claim the work as their own or use it without permission. A watermark doesn't prevent copying outright, but it does make casual misuse more visible and less appealing, and it reinforces attribution wherever the image circulates.</p>
 
   <h3>Choosing the Right Watermark Settings</h3>
