   <p>When two JSON objects contain the same data but their keys are in a different order, a plain text comparison will flag them as different even though they're functionally identical. Sorting keys alphabetically before comparing removes this ordering noise, making it much easier to spot genuine differences between two JSON payloads — for example, when debugging why an API response doesn't match an expected test fixture, or when comparing two versions of a configuration file that were edited independently.</p>
