     <li><strong>Emergency signaling</strong> — SOS (··· --- ···) remains internationally recognized as a distress signal.</li>
@@ -136,21 +164,22 @@
   <p>When decoding Morse code by eye rather than by ear, the key is recognizing that spacing carries as much meaning as the dots and dashes themselves. A single space typically separates individual dots and dashes within one letter, a larger gap separates one complete letter from the next, and an even larger gap separates one word from the next. This tool's input format follows that same convention, using a forward slash to mark word boundaries, which keeps the decoding process unambiguous even for longer messages with multiple words and multiple sentences strung together.</p>
 </section>
 
