   <p>Not every country names large numbers the same way. The short scale, used by this tool and standard across the US, UK, and most English-speaking countries today, defines a billion as a thousand million (1,000,000,000). The long scale, historically used in many European countries, instead defines a billion as a million million (1,000,000,000,000) — what the short scale calls a trillion. Most European countries have since adopted the short scale for everyday use, but the distinction occasionally still causes confusion in translated or historical documents, which is worth keeping in mind for any number translated from a long-scale source.</p>
 
