   <h2>How PDF Merging Works</h2>
   <p>This tool uses PDF-Lib, a JavaScript library that works directly with a PDF's internal page structure rather than converting pages to images and stitching them together. When you merge files, each page from every uploaded PDF is copied — complete with its original text, fonts, images, and vector graphics — into a new combined document, in the exact order you've arranged them. Because pages are copied at the structural level rather than rendered and re-encoded, there's no quality loss anywhere in the process.</p>
 
@@ -136,7 +155,7 @@
