   <h2>About the PDF Rotate Tool</h2>
   <p>The Logrith PDF Rotate tool fixes sideways or upside-down pages in a PDF document without needing to reprint, rescan, or install desktop software. Rotate individual pages, a custom range, odd or even pages only, or the entire document, all directly in your browser. This is one of the most common fixes needed after scanning paper documents, since scanners and multi-function printers frequently produce pages that are rotated 90 or 180 degrees from how they should appear.</p>
 
   <p>A sideways PDF page is a small but genuinely annoying problem — the content is all there, correctly scanned and readable, but viewing or printing it means constantly tilting your head or your printed page. Rather than rescanning the document correctly, which isn't always possible if you no longer have the original paper, rotating the existing PDF pages fixes the orientation in seconds.</p>
 
