   <p>Finding the ideal compression quality for a target file size isn't something you can calculate directly, since file size depends on image content in ways that are hard to predict mathematically in advance. Instead, this tool uses a binary search approach: it tries a quality setting roughly in the middle of the possible range, checks whether the resulting file is above or below the target, then narrows the search to the half of the range that's likely to contain the right answer, repeating this process several times. This converges on a quality setting very close to the maximum achievable within your target size in just a handful of compression attempts, rather than blindly trying many quality levels one at a time.</p>
 
   <h3>Why Forms Enforce File Size Limits</h3>
-  <ul class="feature-list">
