   <p>JPEG compression works by selectively discarding image detail that the human eye is less sensitive to, with the quality setting controlling how aggressively this discarding happens. At high quality settings, very little detail is thrown away and the file stays large but visually near-identical to the original. At low quality settings, significantly more detail is discarded, shrinking the file considerably but introducing visible artifacts — blocky patterns, color banding, and blurred fine detail, especially noticeable around sharp edges and text. This tool searches across this quality range automatically to find the highest setting that still fits your target size, rather than requiring you to guess and manually check each attempt yourself.</p>
