   <h2>About the Regex Tester Tool</h2>
   <p>The Logrith Regex Tester lets you build, test, and debug regular expressions against sample text in real time, showing every match, capture group, and flag effect instantly as you type. Regular expressions are a powerful but notoriously tricky syntax to get right on the first try, and this tool removes the guesswork by showing exactly what a pattern matches before you use it in actual code.</p>
 
   <p>A regular expression (regex) is a sequence of characters that defines a search pattern, used for finding, validating, or extracting text that matches specific rules — email addresses, phone numbers, dates, or any custom text format. Writing regex correctly on the first attempt is difficult even for experienced developers, since small syntax differences can completely change what a pattern matches. Testing interactively, rather than running code repeatedly, is by far the fastest way to get a pattern right.</p>
 
   <h3>Understanding Regex Flags</h3>
-  <ul class="feature-list">
+  <ul>
     <li><strong>g (global)</strong> — finds every match in the text instead of stopping after the first one found.</li>
     <li><strong>i (case insensitive)</strong> — matches letters regardless of uppercase or lowercase, so "Hello" and "hello" are treated the same.</li>
     <li><strong>m (multiline)</strong> — changes how ^ and $ behave, making them match the start and end of each line rather than only the start and end of the entire string.</li>
@@ -147,7 +160,7 @@
