+  <h2 class="mt-32">What is ATS and Why Does It Matter?</h2>
+  <p>ATS (Applicant Tracking System) is software used by over 90% of Fortune 500 companies to automatically screen resumes before a human recruiter ever sees them. If your resume does not pass ATS filters, it gets rejected automatically — regardless of how qualified you are. Studies show that 75% of resumes are rejected by ATS before reaching a recruiter.</p>
