   <h2>About the Slug Generator Tool</h2>
   <p>The Logrith Slug Generator converts any title, heading, or phrase into a clean, URL-safe slug — lowercase, hyphen-separated, and stripped of special characters — ready to use as a page URL, blog post path, or file name. This is a small but genuinely important step in web publishing, since a well-formed slug affects both how search engines interpret a page and how readable the URL looks when shared.</p>
 
   <p>A slug is the part of a URL that identifies a specific page in a human and machine-readable way. For a blog post titled "10 Best Budget Laptops in 2024," a good slug would be "10-best-budget-laptops-2024" — all lowercase, words separated by hyphens, with punctuation removed. This tool automates that conversion, handling capitalization, spacing, punctuation, accented characters, and optional stop-word removal in one step.</p>
 
   <h3>What Makes a Good URL Slug</h3>
-  <ul class="feature-list">
+  <ul>
     <li><strong>Lowercase only.</strong> URLs are technically case-sensitive, and mixing cases creates inconsistency and potential duplicate-content issues if the same page is linked with different capitalization.</li>
     <li><strong>Hyphens between words, not underscores.</strong> Search engines, including Google, treat hyphens as word separators but treat underscores as joining words together into one token, which can hurt how individual keywords in the slug are interpreted.</li>
     <li><strong>No special characters.</strong> Spaces, punctuation, and symbols like &amp;, %, or # either break URLs outright or get encoded into unreadable character sequences, so they should be stripped or replaced.</li>
