   <p>Data size conversion has its own quirk worth understanding: there are two competing standards for units like kilobyte and megabyte. The SI (decimal) standard defines a kilobyte as exactly 1,000 bytes, which is what this tool uses for KB, MB, GB, and TB. The binary standard, used internally by operating systems and reflected in units like KiB, MiB, and GiB, defines a "kibibyte" as 1,024 bytes instead. This is exactly why a hard drive labeled "1TB" by its manufacturer (1,000,000,000,000 bytes, SI standard) shows up as roughly 931GB in your operating system (which measures using the binary standard but often still labels it GB). This converter includes both standards side by side so you can see exactly how a value differs between the two.</p>
 
